    <desc>Set the number of columns and rows of new terminals, or resize a window to a preset size.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Terminal sizes</title>

<p>Some programs need a minimum terminal size to display correctly, and long
  lines are easier to read in wide terminals.</p>

  <p>To resize the current window to a preset size, press the menu button in
  the top-right corner of the window, select
  <gui style="menuitem">Advanced</gui> and one of <gui>80×24</gui>,
  <gui>80×43</gui>, <gui>132×24</gui> and <gui>132×43</gui> columns and
  rows.</p>

  <p>To set the size of new windows:</p>
  <steps>
<item><p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window and select <gui style="menuitem">Preferences</gui>.</p></item><item><p>In the <gui>Profiles</gui> group, click the profile you want to change. Its settings open on a page of their own.</p></item>
<item><p>In the <gui>Terminal Size</gui> group, set the number of <gui>Columns</gui> and <gui>Rows</gui>.</p></item>
</steps>

  <p>New windows can also take the size of the terminal you used last, see
  <link xref="gs-session#window-size"/>.</p>

